{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/matrixorigin/matrixone/pulls/26655","id":4195661308,"node_id":"PR_kwDOFEPiGM76FLX8","html_url":"https://github.com/matrixorigin/matrixone/pull/26655","diff_url":"https://github.com/matrixorigin/matrixone/pull/26655.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/matrixorigin/matrixone/pull/26655.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/matrixorigin/matrixone/issues/26655","number":26655,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"[Feature]: add TAE object lifecycle archive and restore","user":{"login":"LeftHandCold","id":14086886,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MDg2ODg2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/14086886?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeftHandCold","html_url":"https://github.com/LeftHandCold","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeftHandCold/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeftHandCold/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeftHandCold/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeftHandCold/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeftHandCold/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeftHandCold/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeftHandCold/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeftHandCold/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeftHandCold/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## What type of PR is this?\n\n- [ ] API-change\n- [ ] BUG\n- [ ] Improvement\n- [ ] Documentation\n- [x] Feature\n- [x] Test and CI\n- [ ] Code Refactoring\n\n## Which issue(s) this PR fixes:\n\nissue #24853\n\nRelated to #24552\n\n## What this PR does / why we need it:\n\nImplements the Phase 1 TAE Object Lifecycle feature for explicitly bound tables:\n\n- TTL retirement and Archive to immutable Parquet/ZSTD Datasets.\n- Exact Object retirement through the existing TAE Merge, transfer, WAL, Replay, and GC paths; no parallel Merge implementation.\n- Single-source mixed-Object Rewrite, full archive readback verification, and bounded Root-based cleanup.\n- Restore of one Archive Dataset or a half-open table/time range into an independent new table, using a frozen bounded Dataset selection, deterministic chunks, exact row filtering, and idempotent receipts.\n- Bounded SHOW LIFECYCLE RESTORES visibility for Restore state and progress.\n- Fresh-bootstrap and upgrade catalog initialization, release gating, scheduling, observability, BVT coverage, and deterministic fault-injection coverage.\n\n### Scope and compatibility\n\n- The feature is disabled by default and only scans explicitly bound tables.\n- Ordinary query, DML, and normal Merge paths do not read Lifecycle metadata or perform Lifecycle provider I/O.\n- Source data is retired only after archive verification and final atomic publication succeed; unknown final commits remain fail-closed.\n- Range Restore uses the existing Restore Attempt and ordinary MO transactions; it adds no generic transaction subsystem, background task framework, global slot table, or TN permit.\n- Phase 1 excludes ONLINE_COLD, CDC/CCPR integration, archive-aware Backup/DR, Deep Archive, and restore into the original table.\n- Design documents are intentionally excluded from this implementation PR.\n\n### Validation\n\n- Serial targeted tests: Lifecycle, disttae Lifecycle paths, frontend, TAE RPC, engine Restore integration, and generated MySQL parser.\n- Focused range-Restore tests cover half-open boundaries, multi-Dataset selection, frozen retry identity, exact row filtering, lease release, selection drift rejection, and Manifest/Dataset/Chunk resource bounds.\n- Lifecycle race tests and deterministic fault-injection coverage for response loss, commit unknown, restart, late PUT, cleanup, and mixed Rewrite.\n- Isolated full-MO E2E: bootstrap, release gate, TTL, Archive, Manifest/Dataset verification, single-Dataset Restore, restart, mixed Rewrite, and cleanup convergence.\n- Static analysis, build/vet, parser regeneration, make err-check, and git diff --check.\n\nThis PR remains Draft while CI and commercial-scale certification (range-Restore E2E, provider fault matrix, 1/10 TiB, 50 to 1000 bound tables, and long coexistence soak) are completed.\n\n### QA Decision\n\nQA required: yes — archive/restore changes persisted data lifecycle and provider failure handling. Verify retirement only after archive verification and atomic publication, restore row correctness, restart/replay, retention and cleanup. Range-Restore E2E, the provider fault matrix, 1/10 TiB, 50–1000 bound tables and long coexistence soak remain pending as stated above.\n\n\n### Scoped maintenance validation (2026-10-08)\n\nMerged `main@bab4b3286a0dd5683a9b291763817722233e586c` and regenerated conflicted API/parser bindings from the merged sources with repository-pinned protoc21.1, repository goyacc and the required admission-guard postprocessor. Retains current collation/key-format metadata and validation alongside Lifecycle entries. Updated obsolete planner test fixtures to use the current owned process fixture and the exact truncated-array decoder error expectation for Go1.27. Production archive semantics were not changed by this maintenance.\n\nValidation on the final source content (Go1.27, CGO enabled, default SIMD):\n- Full8 owning packages: API, parser subpackages, Lifecycle, plan and compile: PASS.\n- Admission postprocessor tests and normal native/service build: PASS.\n- Canonical `pub_sub4.sql`, including the prepared JDBC primary-key metadata query from the failed CI job:122/122 PASS in each of two runs;0failed/ignored/abnormal. SQL/ISCP readiness and fixture teardown verified; owned service stopped. This is local single-CN evidence, not proof that the entire original multi-CN CI is green.\n- Deterministic generation, source fingerprints and `git diff --check` against the frozen target main: PASS. Two whitespace-bearing charset expected-result lines inherited unchanged from main were preserved (identical file blob).\n\nThe initial missing admission postprocess caused a real API rejection-test failure; obsolete planner constructors failed compilation, and the old JSON decoder expectation failed under Go1.27. Those failures were retained and corrected before final validation. Earlier validation listed above remains historical; it is not automatically transferred to this head. Full archive/provider fault matrix, range-Restore E2E, commercial-scale/soak, mixed-version acceptance and QA remain pending. The PR remains Draft. Related issue: https://github.com/matrixorigin/matrixone/issues/24853.\n","created_at":"2026-08-03T15:21:02Z","updated_at":"2026-10-08T04:47:42Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[{"login":"heni02","id":113406637,"node_id":"U_kgDOBsJyrQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/113406637?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/heni02","html_url":"https://github.com/heni02","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/heni02/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/heni02/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/heni02/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/heni02/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/heni02/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/heni02/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/heni02/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/heni02/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/heni02/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[{"id":3134841077,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwzMTM0ODQxMDc3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/matrixorigin/matrixone/labels/kind/feature","name":"kind/feature","color":"C2E0C6","default":false,"d